Correct colors on big-endian hosts (PowerPC).

ImU32 colors keep imgui's default 0xAABBGGRR value layout everywhere, so all
hard-coded color values in ImHex, the text editor palettes, ImPlot colormaps
and the pattern language palette stay valid. Byte order is only fixed where
colors cross between values and bytes:

- imgui_impl_opengl3: swizzle ImDrawVert::col in the vertex shader and upload
  RGBA32 textures as GL_UNSIGNED_INT_8_8_8_8_REV on big-endian hosts.
- theme parsing/export, bookmark export and the pattern language [[color]]
  attribute: convert RRGGBB(AA) <-> ImU32 with std::byteswap instead of
  changeEndianness(..., big), which is a no-op on big-endian hosts.
- diagram and indexed-image visualizer bitmaps: store u32 pixels as
  little-endian before uploading them as bytes.

Applies on top of patch-legacy-opengl.diff. No change on little-endian hosts.

